## Sources

*.cr text eol=lf

# iyi: `.iyi` is Crystal's grammar with a different compilation model, so GitHub
# should read it the way the compiler does. Without this the samples, which are
# the documentation, render as plain text.
*.iyi text eol=lf linguist-language=Crystal

# iyi: a template's bytes are what `Eiy.embed` renders, and an exercise
# compares the render against a string written in its source. Checked out
# with CRLF — which is what a Windows clone does to a file nothing pins —
# every line of the render gained a byte and
# `bench/std_eiy_exercise.iyi` failed on Windows alone.
*.eiy text eol=lf

# iyi: a gate is a shell script, and a shell script with CRLF is not a
# program: Linux reads `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` as an interpreter it cannot
# find. A Windows clone gives CRLF to anything nothing pins, and an editor
# on Windows gives it back on every save, so 27 gates in `bench/` arrived
# that way in one night's work.
*.sh text eol=lf

# iyi: the design documents are read by line - `bench/doc_numbers.py` quotes
# them by line number, and a diff of one is a review. A Windows save gave
# GC_DESIGN.md CRLF, and a one-line change came in as 1,929.
*.md text eol=lf

# A module artifact is binary. Without this GitHub tries to render one and git
# tries to diff it.
*.iyimod binary

